Subject: [PATCH 1/1] Make the VAD prefix and the Qwen pass separately runnable

Reason: Finoka's cloud deployment rents its accelerator by the second and runs
one FineSub task across three containers. `run_vad_asr` is one process from
energy VAD through Whisper to the Qwen referee, and only the Whisper leg needs
the GPU. This patch splits the other two out as opt-in entry points so they can
run on cheap CPU containers, without changing what any of them computes.

Everything here is additive. `prepare_vad_asr`, `prepared_vad_matches`,
`prepared_vad_has_speech`, `finalize_qwen_verification` and `QwenReferee.warm`
are new, and so are two stdlib imports they need. The only edit to existing
code is the `prepared_path=None` keyword on `run_vad_asr`: its prefix block
moves into an `else:` arm one level deeper, statement for statement, and the
default reaches it. A caller that does not pass the keyword -- every local
run, the CLI, batch -- executes exactly the upstream code path.

`tests/test_split_stage_contract.py` in the Finoka repository enforces that
reading of this patch: two files touched, every deleted statement re-appearing
verbatim modulo indentation, and comments only re-wrapped, never reworded.

Removal: Delete once upstream can run the VAD prefix and the referee as
separate steps, or once Finoka stops splitting the stage across containers.

